Defining Car Detailing
Car detailing is a thorough cleaning and restoration process for both the interior and exterior of a car. It removes dirt, grime, and old wax, then restores shine and adds protection.
Detailing is different from a regular wash in three ways:
It cleans every surface, not just visible dirt
It uses specialized products for paint, glass, leather, and fabric
It adds a protective layer like wax, sealant, or ceramic coating
